    "Requirement Analysis": "We must preserve protocol-required files exactly and build with CMake. Core domain mechanics (bird physics, pipe movement, collision, scoring, game-over, reset) must be implemented in reusable modules. Deterministic tests will drive updates via fixed dt and a seeded RNG boundary. The runtime entry provides a short, non-interactive demo. The architecture separates domain logic from RNG/time/UI and avoids circular dependencies.\n\nPlanned file list (exact paths):\n- CMakeLists.txt\n- include/GameConfig.h, src/GameConfig.cpp\n- include/Random.h, src/Random.cpp\n- include/Bird.h, src/Bird.cpp\n- include/Pipe.h, src/Pipe.cpp\n- include/GameState.h, src/GameState.cpp\n- include/GameEngine.h, src/GameEngine.cpp\n- src/Main.cpp\n- tests/test_main.cpp\n\nAllowed include direction (no cycles):\n- GameEngine.h/.cpp -> GameState.h, GameConfig.h, Random.h\n- GameState.h/.cpp -> Bird.h, Pipe.h, GameConfig.h, Random.h (via forward interface)\n- Bird.h/.cpp -> GameConfig.h\n- Pipe.h/.cpp -> GameConfig.h\n- Random.h/.cpp -> <no domain includes>\n- Main.cpp -> GameEngine.h, GameConfig.h, Random.h\n- tests/test_main.cpp -> GameEngine.h, GameConfig.h, Random.h\n\nDependency-ordered Task list with role ownership (Bob, Eve, Alex):\n1) CMakeLists.txt [Alex]\n- Define project with C++17, two executables: flappy_demo (src/Main.cpp + src/*.cpp) and tests (tests/test_main.cpp). Enable CTest and add test that runs the single test target.\n\n2) include/Random.h [Bob]\n- Declare canonical RNG boundary.\n- API: class IRandom { virtual ~IRandom(); virtual double nextUnit()=0; }.\n- API: class LcgRandom : public IRandom { explicit LcgRandom(uint64_t seed); double nextUnit() override; uint64_t nextUint64(); }.\n- Semantics: nextUnit returns [0,1) deterministically; nextUint64 returns the raw sequence.\n\n3) src/Random.cpp [Bob]\n- Implement LCG with 64-bit state: state = (a*state + c) mod 2^64, standard constants (e.g., a=6364136223846793005, c=1). Convert to double in [0,1).\n- Validate via simple non-throwing behavior; no external deps.\n\n4) include/GameConfig.h [Bob]\n- Declare struct GameConfig with gameplay constants: worldWidth, worldHeight, gravity, flapImpulse, maxFallSpeed, pipeSpeed, pipeWidth, pipeGapHeight, pipeSpawnInterval, birdX, birdWidth, birdHeight.\n- Provide static GameConfig Default(); void validate() const; equality comparators not required.\n- Document error behavior: validate throws std::invalid_argument on invalid values.\n\n5) src/GameConfig.cpp [Bob]\n- Implement Default() with reasonable deterministic values (e.g., width=400, height=300, gravity=900 px/s^2, flapImpulse=300 px/s, maxFallSpeed=600 px/s, pipeSpeed=80 px/s, pipeWidth=40 px, pipeGapHeight=120 px, pipeSpawnInterval=1.5 s, birdX=80 px, birdWidth=24 px, birdHeight=18 px).\n- Implement validate(): ensure all positives where applicable, birdX within world.\n\n6) include/Bird.h [Eve]\n- Declare class Bird with private double y_, v_; non-owning constants taken from GameConfig.\n- API: Bird(double y0, double v0);\n- void flap(const GameConfig& cfg);\n- void update(double dt, const GameConfig& cfg);\n- double y() const; double velocity() const; double top(const GameConfig& cfg) const; double bottom(const GameConfig& cfg) const;\n- void reset(double y0);\n- Semantics: flap adds upward impulse to velocity (negative up or positive up depending convention; choose positive up and apply gravity downward), update clamps within world bounds and caps fall speed.\n\n7) src/Bird.cpp [Eve]\n- Implement physics: v_ += flapImpulse on flap; update: v_ -= gravity*dt; clamp v_ >= -maxFallSpeed if using up-positive; y_ += v_*dt; clamp y_ within [birdHeight/2, worldHeight - birdHeight/2].\n- Provide top/bottom using birdHeight.\n\n8) include/Pipe.h [Eve]\n- Declare struct Pipe { double x; double gapY; bool scored; }.\n- API: Pipe(double x0, double gapY0);\n- void update(double dt, const GameConfig& cfg);\n- bool isOffscreen(const GameConfig& cfg) const;\n- bool hasPassedBird(double birdX, const GameConfig& cfg) const;\n- bool collidesWithBird(double birdX, double birdTop, double birdBottom, const GameConfig& cfg) const;\n- Semantics: gapY is center of gap; collision checks if bird rectangle overlaps either top or bottom pipe rectangle.\n\n9) src/Pipe.cpp [Eve]\n- Implement horizontal movement: x -= pipeSpeed*dt.\n- isOffscreen: x + pipeWidth < 0.\n- hasPassedBird: (x + pipeWidth) < birdX.\n- collidesWithBird: compute pipe rectangles: top: [x, x+pipeWidth] x [0, gapY - gapHeight/2]; bottom: [x, x+pipeWidth] x [gapY + gapHeight/2, worldHeight]; check overlap with bird rectangle [birdX - birdWidth/2, birdX + birdWidth/2] x [birdTop, birdBottom].\n\n10) include/GameState.h [Alex]\n- Declare class GameState encapsulating Bird, pipes, score, gameOver, timeSinceLastPipe.\n- API: explicit GameState(const GameConfig& cfg);\n- void reset();\n- void flap();\n- void update(double dt, IRandom& rng);\n- int score() const; bool gameOver() const;\n- const std::vector<Pipe>& pipes() const; double birdY() const; double birdTop() const; double birdBottom() const;\n- Semantics: update advances bird and pipes if not gameOver; spawns new pipes when timer exceeds spawn interval with gapY determined via rng; scoring when pipes pass bird; set gameOver on collision or out-of-bounds.\n\n11) src/GameState.cpp [Alex]\n- Implement constructor with initial bird centered vertically and cleared pipes.\n- Implement spawn logic: gapY = clamp((rng.nextUnit()*(worldHeight - pipeGapHeight)) + pipeGapHeight/2), x = worldWidth.\n- Implement per-tick: decrement timer, spawn as needed; update pipes; remove offscreen pipes; scoring set once per pipe via hasPassedBird; collision detection via collidesWithBird.\n\n12) include/GameEngine.h [Alex]\n- Declare class GameEngine that owns GameConfig and IRandom (via unique_ptr) and a GameState instance.\n- API: explicit GameEngine(GameConfig cfg, std::unique_ptr<IRandom> rng);\n- void reset();\n- void flap();\n- void step(double dt);\n- int score() const; bool isGameOver() const; double birdY() const; const std::vector<Pipe>& pipes() const; const GameConfig& config() const;\n- Semantics: thin wrapper delegating to GameState with provided RNG; guards calls when gameOver.\n\n13) src/GameEngine.cpp [Alex]\n- Implement all methods; validate config via cfg.validate() in constructor; on reset() rebuild GameState.\n\n14) src/Main.cpp [Alex]\n- Non-interactive demo: construct GameEngine with GameConfig::Default() and LcgRandom(seed=42); run a short simulation for ~5 seconds with fixed dt (e.g., 0.02 s), apply flaps at deterministic intervals (e.g., every 0.6 s); print final score and game over state; exit.\n- No loops that wait for input; no graphics.\n\n15) tests/test_main.cpp [Alex]\n- Include headers: GameEngine.h, GameConfig.h, Random.h.\n- Test 1: Bird physics: after a flap and a few steps, birdY increases initially, then decreases due to gravity; assert monotonic behaviors at specific ticks.\n- Test 2: Scoring: simulate enough ticks with periodic flaps to avoid crash; assert score increments when a pipe passes.\n- Optional Test 3: Collision and reset: force no flaps and high gravity to collide; assert gameOver becomes true, then reset returns to gameOver false and score zero.\n\nCanonical Public API spec (modules, signatures, semantics):\n- include/Random.h:\n  - struct IRandom { virtual ~IRandom() noexcept = default; virtual double nextUnit() = 0; }.\n    Returns a deterministic pseudorandom double in [0,1); no exceptions.\n  - class LcgRandom : public IRandom {\n      explicit LcgRandom(uint64_t seed);\n      double nextUnit() override;\n      uint64_t nextUint64();\n    }.\n    Deterministic 64-bit LCG; nextUnit = nextUint64 / 2^64; no exceptions.\n\n- include/GameConfig.h:\n  - struct GameConfig {\n      double worldWidth, worldHeight;\n      double gravity, flapImpulse, maxFallSpeed;\n      double pipeSpeed, pipeWidth, pipeGapHeight, pipeSpawnInterval;\n      double birdX, birdWidth, birdHeight;\n      static GameConfig Default();\n      void validate() const;\n    }.\n    Default provides sane parameters; validate throws std::invalid_argument when any non-positive, invalid ranges, or birdX out of bounds.\n\n- include/Bird.h:\n  - class Bird {\n      Bird(double y0, double v0);\n      void flap(const GameConfig& cfg);\n      void update(double dt, const GameConfig& cfg);\n      double y() const;\n      double velocity() const;\n      double top(const GameConfig& cfg) const;\n      double bottom(const GameConfig& cfg) const;\n      void reset(double y0);\n    }.\n    Physics: positive up velocity; gravity reduces velocity; clamp position to playfield.\n\n- include/Pipe.h:\n  - struct Pipe {\n      double x; double gapY; bool scored;\n      explicit Pipe(double x0, double gapY0);\n      void update(double dt, const GameConfig& cfg);\n      bool isOffscreen(const GameConfig& cfg) const;\n      bool hasPassedBird(double birdX, const GameConfig& cfg) const;\n      bool collidesWithBird(double birdX, double birdTop, double birdBottom, const GameConfig& cfg) const;\n    }.\n    Movement left at pipeSpeed; collision if bird rectangle overlaps non-gap regions.\n\n- include/GameState.h:\n  - class GameState {\n      explicit GameState(const GameConfig& cfg);\n      void reset();\n      void flap();\n      void update(double dt, IRandom& rng);\n      int score() const;\n      bool gameOver() const;\n      const std::vector<Pipe>& pipes() const;\n      double birdY() const;\n      double birdTop() const;\n      double birdBottom() const;\n    }.\n    Drives all domain updates; spawn pipes via rng; scoring and collision rules; frozen when gameOver.\n\n- include/GameEngine.h:\n  - class GameEngine {\n      explicit GameEngine(GameConfig cfg, std::unique_ptr<IRandom> rng);\n      void reset();\n      void flap();\n      void step(double dt);\n      int score() const;\n      bool isGameOver() const;\n      double birdY() const;\n      const std::vector<Pipe>& pipes() const;\n      const GameConfig& config() const;\n    }.\n    Facade over GameState; coordinates config validation and RNG ownership.\n\nThese APIs are the only public surface used by runtime and tests. Error behavior is limited to GameConfig::validate throwing invalid_argument; other methods avoid throwing under normal use.",
